"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","title":"Interaction_DragView"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/alignmentGuide(_:computeValue:)-9thl1":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/alignmentGuide(_:computeValue:)-9thl1","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/alignmentguide(_:computevalue:)-9thl1","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"alignmentGuide"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"VerticalAlignment","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI17VerticalAlignmentV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"computeValue"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ViewDimensions","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI14ViewDimensionsV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CGFloat","preciseIdentifier":"s:14CoreFoundation7CGFloatV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"View","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"alignmentGuide(_:computeValue:)"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Swami","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}]}}}